**when to use git init?**

1. when starting a new project from scratch
    mkdir git-project
    cd git-project
    git init
2. when converting an existing folder into git repo
   cd old-project
   git init
   git add .
3. when creating a new repo that you will later push to github
   git init
   git add .
   git commit -m "commit message"

**when not to use git init**

1. when you clone git already does the initialization for you
git clone "htps://"
it automatically creates a folder run git init internally adds a remote origin downloads all commits and branches

2. when you are already inside git repo
if the folder already .git directory never run git init
