**Merge conflict:**

if two branches have different content when you are doing it shows merge conflict

For example, we have index.html in master branch if we chnage index.html in something else and developers branch index.html have different content then we try to merge we get conflict because smae files but content is different.

✅ STEP-1: Go to master branch
git checkout master
✅ STEP-2: Edit the SAME LINE in index.html
Example:
In master, open file:
vi index.html
Change the first line to:
<h1>Version from MASTER</h1>
Save, then:
git add index.html
git commit -m "master version"
git push
✅ STEP-3: Go to developers branch
git checkout developers
Edit the SAME EXACT line again:
vi index.html
Change the same line to:
<h1>Version from DEVELOPERS</h1>
Save, commit, push:
git add index.html
git commit -m "developers version"
git push
⚠️ Now master and developers have conflicting lines.
Both changed the same line differently.
✅ STEP-4: Try to merge developers → master
git checkout master
git merge developers

